From: Ubuntu Embedded Team <ljzyx86@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: honor recovery before distro boot

Apply after 0001-rockchip-extlinux-fdtoverlays.patch. A BCB or reboot
recovery request must select the vendor recovery loader before extlinux
can boot the normal system. Change only the in-memory bootcmd, never
persist a recovery override to the environment.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -259,6 +259,10 @@
 		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; download");
 		run_command("download", 0);
 		break;
+	case BOOT_MODE_RECOVERY:
+		/* Recovery must bypass the normal distro/extlinux path. */
+		env_set("bootcmd", RKIMG_VENDOR_BOOTCOMMAND);
+		break;
 	case BOOT_MODE_CHARGING:
 		printf("enter charging!\n");
 		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; charge");
